---
/**
 * Ancestral sampling from a continuous-time diffusion model, running live
 * with the exact score of a known Gaussian mixture, so the sampler can be
 * graded on mode coverage instead of admired for producing plausible points.
 */
import { WEIGHTS } from '../sim/mixture.js';

const label =
  'Live simulation: 640 samples being generated by the reverse-time SDE of a ' +
  'variance-preserving diffusion model, integrated from t = 1 to t = 0. The ' +
  'samples begin as an isotropic Gaussian and separate onto the six modes of ' +
  'the target Gaussian mixture, in proportion to its unequal mixture weights ' +
  '0.28, 0.22, 0.17, 0.14, 0.11 and 0.08. Color encodes the data-space ' +
  'energy minus log p-zero on the cividis colormap, and faint contours of the ' +
  'same energy are drawn underneath. At the end of each pass the recovered ' +
  'mixture weights are compared with the true ones.';
---

<figure class="figure">
  <div class="figure-frame sampler" data-sim="diffusion" role="img" aria-label={label}>
    <picture data-poster>
      <source srcset="/poster/diffusion-dark.avif" type="image/avif" media="(prefers-color-scheme: dark)" />
      <source srcset="/poster/diffusion-dark.webp" type="image/webp" media="(prefers-color-scheme: dark)" />
      <source srcset="/poster/diffusion-light.avif" type="image/avif" />
      <img src="/poster/diffusion-light.webp" width="1200" height="600" alt="" decoding="async" loading="lazy" />
    </picture>
    <canvas data-layer="contours" hidden aria-hidden="true"></canvas>
    <canvas data-layer="particles" hidden aria-hidden="true"></canvas>
    <div class="readout" data-readout aria-hidden="true">
      <span>t&nbsp;=&nbsp;<b data-t>0.00</b></span>
      <span>step&nbsp;<b data-step>320/320</b></span>
      <span>max|ŵ−w|&nbsp;=&nbsp;<b data-grade>0.026</b></span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <figcaption class="figure-caption">
    <b>Fig. 2.</b> Ancestral sampling from a continuous-time diffusion model. The
    forward variance-preserving SDE noises a six-component Gaussian mixture into
    <span class="nowrap">𝒩(0, I)</span>; the reverse SDE carries 640 samples back over 320
    Euler–Maruyama steps. Because a mixture stays a mixture under the VP kernel, the
    score used here is exact rather than learned, which leaves discretization as the
    only source of error and turns the mixture weights into something gradable. True
    weights <span class="nowrap">({WEIGHTS.join(', ')})</span>; the readout reports
    <span class="nowrap">max<sub>k</sub> |ŵ<sub>k</sub> − w<sub>k</sub>|</span> at the end of
    each pass, against a Monte Carlo floor of 0.018 at n = 640. Color and contours
    encode <span class="nowrap">−log p₀</span>.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .sampler { aspect-ratio: 2 / 1; }
  .sampler .readout { bottom: auto; top: 0; border-top: 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); }
  .nowrap { white-space: nowrap; }
</style>

<script>
  import '../scripts/diffusion.client.js';
</script>
